Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: whykey
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: python3
Description: explain where a Linux key combination is handled
 Whykey diagnoses the path of a keyboard event through Linux desktops,
 terminals, TTYs, multiplexers, shells, and supported applications.
 It never edits configuration files or executes the shortcut under
 investigation.
 .
 The optional whykey-nvim, whykey-vscode, and whykey-emacs editor
 extensions are Python 3 scripts and need python3 (recommended).
